Every star the IAU has named, from the IAU Catalog of Star Names kept by its Working Group on Star Names (WGSN). Each star is listed by its Hipparcos number: Vega is Nam 91262. 578 stars carry 579 names. The 73 names of objects without a Hipparcos number, mostly faint planet-host stars, are left out. Epsilon Bootis (Nam 72105) has two IAU names, Izar and Pulcherrima, and the IAU does not say which star of the pair each one names, so neither is shown as its name.
